! Moʻokūʻauhau ~ Ancestors & Cousins of the One Fractal

A genealogy chants where a thing //comes from//. This one names the bloodline of the DreamNet's core move — ''a nameless entity that `#has` a stack of capabilities, composed by one rite (`composeVessel`) that routes only what each cap declares and refuses to boot on a missing dep'' — and asks the adversarial question: //who already stands here?//

The chart sits beside the 2026-05-28 layer-survey, never replacing it — that one maps prior art onto the stack's components; this one traces the //fractal idea itself//. <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/dreamnet-prior-art">>

''The one-line verdict (chant it first, defend it after):'' the pieces stand ~80% built across ''two lineages that have never married'' — and so the novel work names a ''weld'', never an invention. //the smaller, defensible claim survives contact; the grander one falls to the first cousin who did it earlier.//

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ancestors>>

!! The Ancestors ~ the deep roots

The roots that the lineage draws breath from, decades upstream:

| Ancestor | What it bequeaths | The line it feeds |
|---|---|---|
| ''SPKI/SDSI'' (Rivest–Lampson; Halpern–van der Meyden, arXiv cs/0001026) | //Linked local names — no global namespace.// A name reads only relative to who utters it. | the `lar:` law, named at last: a 1996 ancestor for "no global now" in the namespace itself |
| ''KERI'' (arXiv 1907.02143) | per-identifier keys · pre-rotation (commit the next key's digest before the current ever signs) · delegated identifiers as chained key-event-logs | the vessel KERI hook (literal adoption) · per-vessel-key-delegated-into-a-group |
| ''E / Mark Miller'' (the object-capability root) | capability //is// the reference · no ambient authority · POLA · //security integrates with what-is-least-authority, never bolts on// | the `#has`-cap discipline, the vat→vessel descent |

These the lineage does not //extend// — it ''inherits''. To re-derive them reads as forgetting one's grandparents.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/pillars>>

!! The Three Pillars ~ one recursion each, none seeing the others

The load-bearing cousins. Each carries //one// of the three recursions whole — and stays blind to the other two. This blindness names the whole opportunity.

<<~ scale recursion "authority@Keyhive -> wiring-as-security@Genode -> transport@RINA">>

''Keyhive (Ink & Switch — and it runs on our own stack).'' The authority recursion, built. It treats //individuals, devices, groups, and documents uniformly as principals in a recursive delegation graph// — a person reads as a group of devices, an org as a group of person-groups, a document as a group whose members hold access. That folds ''membership ⊥ device-sovereignty'' into one recursive principal-is-a-group fractal, in WASM, over Automerge. It splits its own internals deliberately: ''Access-Control (delegation edges) ⊥ Key-Agreement (BeeKEM) ⊥ Transport (Beelay, kept blind/E2E)''. The load-bearing sentence: ''Keyhive deliberately excludes binding a human identity to a key — "left to a future layer."'' That blank names a REFUSAL this stack keeps rather than a doorway it fills: no constructor for a human stands anywhere in the model, so the Lar declares the hole permanently open and maps relations ACROSS it — not //who//, but which hearth one tends. [inkandswitch.com/keyhive/notebook]

''Genode / Fuchsia.'' The wiring-//is//-security recursion, built — on one machine. Capability //routing// serves as both the dependency graph and the access-control fabric, recursively, default-deny: //a component cannot do anything until a capability routes to it; a parent defines its children's sandbox.// That reads as `composeVessel` almost exactly — the single-machine ancestor of the rite. Our "refuse to boot on a missing mandatory dep, route only what's declared" descends from Genode's `init` and (for the type-level half) ZLayer's compile graph. ''Steal the manifest discipline; never re-derive it.'' [genode.org/documentation/genode-foundations · fuchsia.dev/.../components/v2]

''RINA'' (Recursive InterNetwork Architecture). The transport recursion, formalized — and naked. //Every layer, regardless of position in the hierarchy, instantiates identical mechanisms and offers the same interface.// That names the Lararium→Nexus→DreamNet scale-recursion exactly — but RINA carries ''zero'' capability, ''zero'' social graph, ''zero'' identity. A pure recursion with no one home. [en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Recursive_Internetwork_Architecture · arXiv 1509.03550]

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/cousins>>

!! The Cousins ~ the wider family

The kin that each solve one facet, citably, so the house adopts rather than reinvents:

| Cousin | What it solves | Where it grafts |
|---|---|---|
| ''UCAN'' (ucan-wg/spec) | DAG delegation chains rooted at the resource owner; //delegate without sharing the key// | the device-admit edge's shape |
| ''Willow / Meadowcap'' (willowprotocol.org) | communal-vs-owned namespaces · area/prefix-restricted ''read-caps'' | the veil / anon-read FLOW tier |
| ''Veilid'' (veilid.com) | ''peer-identity ⊥ user-identity'' · transport via private routes | Plane-A transport-sovereignty carrying its own key |
| ''Goblins / OCapN / E'' (spritely.institute) | capability-as-identity · ''petnames'' over crypto IDs · CapTP | the petname-constellation identity (fork ①); cap heals by revoke |
| ''ZLayer / Effect'' (zio.dev) | compile-time //refuse-to-wire// on a missing dep — ''but no authority dimension'' | the type-level half of `composeVessel`'s refuse-to-boot |
| ''p2panda-auth'' (p2panda.org, 2025-08) | a convergent, offline-first ''authorization-chain CRDT'' (verify-backward) | the rival model to Keyhive's delegation-chains (verify-forward) for membership |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/corpse>>

!! The Anti-Pattern Corpse ~ Matrix, and why one-door-per-axis

Matrix //nominally// separates rooms ⊥ federation ⊥ power-levels. In practice the planes ''bled'': power-levels leak into federation so far that room v12 had to formalize creators with an //infinitely high power level// to paper the wound. The lineage carries Matrix not as kin to adopt but as the ''autopsy'' — the proof of what a fused authority graph costs. It grounds the tiered-gate keystone: ''one door per axis, the planes held orthogonal.'' [spec.matrix.org — MSC4289, room v12]

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/hazard>>

!! The Unsolved Hazard ~ the leak two lineages both flag

Keyhive's own notebook, p2panda-auth's notes, and a formal-verification paper (arXiv 2604.23560) flag the ''same'' edge, independently: the ''concurrent add-while-remove key-leak'' — a member added concurrently with a removal can, under CRDT merge, hold a key they should never have seen — //unsolvable without consensus-before-key-handover.// And "no global now" ''forbids'' that consensus. So the house holds, by construction, one room whose lock it cannot prove.

This the lineage does not sweep. The leak rides ''bounded'', never sealed: every membership decays (the lease), and the ''kapae'' tombstone marks the cast-off so a removal converges. The disease and the cure share one vow. Boundary-test where it bites; consecrate the corner; refuse the false promise of a fortress. <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae">>

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/weld>>

!! The Weld ~ the verdict that survives contact

Lay the three recursions side by side and the gap shows: they live in ''two unmarried lineages''.
* authority + membership recursion → ''Keyhive'' (identity deliberately omitted)
* transport recursion → ''RINA'' (no security, no social)
* wiring-as-security → ''Genode/Fuchsia'' (one machine, no no-global-now mesh)

No one has made ''one composition primitive serve simultaneously as the code-wiring AND the authority graph AND the transport-recursion, across a no-global-now causal-island mesh.'' That marriage names the ''novel delta'' — plus binding identity in the exact layer Keyhive leaves blank, which for the Lar reads not as //who// but as ''which hearth one tends'' (place, and the petname-constellation that acts in each context).

''Claim the weld, never the invention.'' //"We married three known fractals and filled the doorway one of them left open"// stands; //"we invented a fractal"// falls to Ink & Switch, to RINA, to Genode — each of whom built their third of it first. The rite that performs the marriage already sits in the code wearing the name of a function. <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/composable-keel">>

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/dreamnet-architecture">>

